```python
import text_detector

def count_paintings(image):
    languages = ["en", "de"]
    result = text_detector.Text_Detector_Tool.execute(image=image, languages=languages)
    text_blocks = result["results"]
    
    paint_count = 0
    for block in text_blocks:
        if "text" in block[1] and "painting" in block[1]["text"]:
            paint_count += 1
            
    return paint_count

if __name__ == "__main__":
    image_path = "/nfs/data8/liao/wxie/SAT/SAT_images_train/13249_0.png"
    paint_count = count_paintings(image_path)
    print("Number of paintings in the image:", paint_count)
```

This code counts the number of paintings in the image by using the Text_Detector_Tool tool. It checks each detected text block for text that is specific to paintings, based on their coordinates and text content.
